                <p class="snippet" >
                     Droit de la famille — 231579, 2023 QCCS 3557, aff’d 2023 QCCA 1547; F.S. v. M.B.T., 2023 ONCJ 102, 89 R.F.L. (8th) 442; Levely v. Levely, 2013 ONSC 1026; <b>Miglin v. Miglin</b>, 2003 SCC 24, [2003] 1 S.C.R. 303; Re T (adult: refusal of medical treatment), [1992] 4 All E.R. 649; Wainwright v. Home Office, [2003] UKHL 53, [2004] 2&nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;As the Court recognized in <b>Miglin v. Miglin</b>, 2003 SCC 24, [2003] 1 S.C.R. 303, at para. 212, “a legacy of abuse” can “colour the parties’ interactions”, even after the relationship ends. 
                </p>
